Tidewave is a coding agent for web application development.  Unlike agents
that only read your source, it connects to your running application, so it
can query the database, inspect logs, evaluate code in the live runtime and
drive the browser while it works.  Phoenix and Rails are supported.

This is the desktop application.  It runs as a system tray icon, supervises
the Tidewave server and offers a menu for opening the web interface in your
browser, editing the configuration and viewing logs.

The command line interface is packaged separately as www/tidewave-cli.
